## 4. System Architecture

```text
                 CUSTOMER / AGENT / ADMIN
                            |
                            v
                       POSTMAN / CLIENT
                            |
                            v
                  SPRING BOOT REST APIs
                            |
                            v
                 SPRING SECURITY + JWT
                            |
                            v
                     SERVICE LAYER
                            |
          +-----------------+------------------+
          |                 |                  |
          v                 v                  v
    Ticket Module      SLA Module         AI Services
          |                 |                  |
          v                 v                  v
    Assignment         SLA Scheduler       Ollama LLM
    Comments           Escalation          Llama 3.2
    History            Analytics           Chatbot / RAG
          |                 |                  |
          +-----------------+------------------+
                            |
                            v
                    SPRING DATA JPA
                            |
                            v
                         MYSQL
```

### Architecture Explanation

1. Client applications send HTTP requests to Spring Boot REST endpoints.
2. Spring Security validates JWT tokens and user permissions.
3. Controllers handle incoming requests.
4. Service classes implement business logic.
5. Spring Data JPA and Hibernate communicate with MySQL.
6. Ollama provides local LLM capabilities for AI-related operations.
7. Scheduled services monitor SLA deadlines and trigger escalations.

